A Samsung TV owner had no page to install from: the app is the browser
client packaged for Tizen, sideloaded and signed per set, and nothing in
the docs said how. The page walks the four steps an owner takes — browser
streaming on the host, Developer Mode on the set, Apps2Samsung or the CLI
route, pair by Request access — and the field traps the first install hit:
the per-set certificate, sideloads lost to a firmware update, the Frame's
refusal. The clients index and the install table link it.
